@meta
id: 05-10
title: Drill — count, jump, insert
chapter: 05
type: drill
skills: word-counts, word-w
par: 15
minutes: 4
reps: 8
vscode: click between two words
open: invoice.md

@brief
Eight times: put `tax, ` in front of `shipping`, so the line ends
`does not include tax, shipping or duty`.

Count first, jump once, insert. No exploratory presses.

@keys
| `6w` | six words forward |
| `i` | insert before the cursor |

@hints
`shipping` is the sixth word after `The`.
--
The rep is not over when the text is right — it is over when you counted
to six without your lips moving.

@solution
    6w  i tax,  <Esc>  :wq<Enter>

Thirteen keystrokes. What you are drilling is not `w`, which you already
have. It is the half-second of looking at a line and knowing it is six,
without walking the cursor along to find out.

That estimate is the skill. Everything from here — counts on operators,
counts on searches, counts on line jumps — leans on being able to look at
text and get a small number right.

@start invoice.md
The order total does not include shipping or duty.

@expected invoice.md
The order total does not include tax, shipping or duty.
